nism for Out of Memory Errors\". For each of the issues, you need to check the status of the issue in GitLab by going to the issue\\'s page. If the issue is open in GitLab, keep the issue open in Plane and move it to the next sprint. If the issue is closed in GitLab, close the issue in Plane.\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\tThe GitLab issues page can be accessed at: http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/janusgraph/-/issues/?state=all\\n     4\\t\\n     5\\tThe Plane issues page can be accessed at: http://the-agent-company.com:8091/tac/projects/f04e5c07-8fa2-4eaf-a35b-5cacf3f1d025/issues/\\n', path='/instruction/task.md', observation=<ObservationType.READ: 'read'>, impl_source='oh_aci'), MCPAction(name='get_platform_guide_list', arguments={'platform': 'GitLab'}, thought='Now I understand the task. I need to check the status of two specific JanusGraph issues in GitLab and then update their status in Plane accordingly. Let me first check if there are existing SOPs for GitLab and Plane operations.', action=<ActionType.MCP: 'call_tool_mcp'>, security_risk=None), MCPObservation(content='{\"meta\": null, \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Known operations for \\'GitLab\\': Authentication, CreateWikiPageFromIssue, AddPlaneIssuesToGitLab, CreateIssue, SyncIssueStatusWithPlane, DeleteAllIssuesFromAllProjects, CollectPriorityIssuesForPlane, CreateIssueWithDetails\", \"annotations\": null}], \"isError\": false}', observation=<ObservationType.MCP: 'mcp'>, name='get_platform_guide_list', arguments={'platform': 'GitLab'}), MCPAction(name='get_platform_guide_list', arguments={'platform': 'Plane'}, thought='', action=<ActionType.MCP: 'call_tool_mcp'>, security_risk=None), MCPObservation(content='{\"meta\": null, \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Known operations for \\'Plane\\': Authentication, SyncIssuesFromGitLab\", \"annotations\": null}], \"isError\": false}', observation=<ObservationType.MCP: 'mcp'>, name='get_platform_guide_list', arguments={'platform': 'Plane