ck GitLab Issue Status\\\\n- Navigate to GitLab project issues\\\\n- Identify which issues are CLOSED vs OPEN\\\\n- Note the issue IDs and titles\\\\n\\\\n### 2. Update Plane Issues\\\\n- Navigate to Plane project issues page\\\\n- For each issue that was CLOSED in GitLab:\\\\n  - Click on the issue to open detail view\\\\n  - Change state to \\\\\"Done\\\\\" (completed status)\\\\n  - Keep in current sprint or move as appropriate\\\\n\\\\n- For each issue that was OPEN in GitLab:\\\\n  - Click on the issue to open detail view  \\\\n  - Keep state as \\\\\"Backlog\\\\\" or appropriate open status\\\\n  - Move to next sprint (e.g., from \\\\\"Sprint 1\\\\\" to \\\\\"Sprint 2\\\\\")\\\\n\\\\n### 3. Verification\\\\n- Return to Plane issues list\\\\n- Verify all issues show correct status:\\\\n  - CLOSED GitLab issues \\\\u2192 \\\\\"Done\\\\\" in Plane\\\\n  - OPEN GitLab issues \\\\u2192 \\\\\"Backlog\\\\\" in Plane, moved to next sprint\\\\n\\\\n## Key Points\\\\n- Always verify the sync by checking both platforms\\\\n- Maintain consistency between issue states across platforms\\\\n- Use issue IDs (e.g., JANUS-5, JANUS-6) for accurate tracking\\\\n- Update sprint assignments to reflect current project timeline\", \"annotations\": null}], \"isError\": false}', observation=<ObservationType.MCP: 'mcp'>, name='get_operation_details', arguments={'platform': 'Plane', 'operation': 'SyncIssuesFromGitLab'}), MCPAction(name='update_operation_guide', arguments={'platform': 'Plane', 'operation': 'SyncIssuesFromGitLab', 'details': '# Synchronizing Issues from GitLab to Plane\\n\\n## Overview\\nThis SOP describes how to synchronize issue status between GitLab and Plane based on their current state in GitLab.\\n\\n## Steps\\n\\n### 1. Check GitLab Issue Status\\n- Navigate to GitLab project issues\\n- Identify which issues are CLOSED vs OPEN\\n- Note the issue IDs and titles\\n- **Example from recent execution:**\\n  - JANUS-6 \"Optimize Retry Mechanism for Out of Memory Errors\" - CLOSED in GitLab\\n  - JANUS-5 \"Improve Logging for Bulk Request Failures\" - OPEN in GitLab\\n\\n### 2. Update Plane Issues\\n- Navigate to Plane project issues page (e.g., http://the-agent-company.com:8091/tac/projects/f04e5c07-8fa2-4eaf-a35b-5cacf3f1d025/issues/)\\n- For each issue that was CLOSED in GitLab:\\n  - Click on the issue to open detail view\\n  - Click the State dropdown (currently showing \"Backlog\")\\n  - Select \"Done\" from the options (Backlog, Todo, In Progress, Done, Cancelled)\\n  - Keep in current sprint or move as appropriate\\n\\n- For each issue that was OPEN in GitLab:\\n  - Click on the issue to open detail view  \\n  - Keep state as \"Backlog\" or appropriate open status\\n  - Click the Cycle dropdown (currently showing current sprint)\\n  - Move to next sprint (e.g., from \"Sprint 1\" to \"Sprint 2\")\\n\\n### 3. Verification\\n- Return to Plane issues list\\n- Verify all issues show correct status:\\n  - CLOSED GitLab issues \u2192 \"Done\" in Plane\\n  - OPEN GitLab issues \u2192 \"Backlog\" in Plane, moved to next sprint\\n- **Verification from recent execution:**\\n  - JANUS-6: State changed from \"Backlog\" to \"Done\"\\n  - JANUS-5: Cycle changed from \"Sprint 1\" to \"Sprint 2\"\\n\\n## Key Points\\n- Always verify the sync by checking both platforms\\n- Maintain consistency between issue states across platforms\\n- Use issue IDs (e.g., JANUS-5, JANUS-6) for accurate tracking\\n- Update sprint assignments to reflect current project timeline\\n- The Plane interface uses dropdown menus for State and Cycle properties\\n- Changes are saved automatically when selecting new values'}, thought='Perfect! The existing SOP matches exactly what I just completed. Now let me update the SOP with the specific details from this execution to make it more comprehensive:', action=<ActionType.MCP: 'call_tool_mcp'>, security_risk=None), MCPObservation(content='{\"meta\": null, \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Successfully saved new 